From: edde746 <86283021+edde746@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vd_lavc: one hwdec thread by default on Apple platforms

The VideoToolbox hwaccels declare neither of libavcodec's thread-safety
caps, so frame threads parse and decode one packet at a time under a
shared lock, and VT decodes each frame in one synchronous call. Extra
threads only let the next packet's header parsing overlap the player's
own work between decode calls. Each one also delays output by a frame
and keeps another decoded surface alive for the length of the pipeline:
three 20 MB P010 surfaces at 4K with the default of 4. Default
--hwdec-threads to 1 on Apple platforms, where VideoToolbox is the only
hardware decoder; software decoding, including the fallback from a
failed hwdec, keeps its own --vd-lavc-threads.

On an iPhone Air the maximum decode rate with 1 and 4 threads is 132.0
and 131.3 fps for 4K HEVC at 90 Mb/s, 144.4 and 143.1 fps for 4K60 HEVC
at 80 Mb/s with 8 B-frames, 424 and 402 fps for 1080p H.264, and 108
and 101 fps with videotoolbox-copy. The footprint drops 34% at 1080p
and 20% at 4K, startup and seeks get faster, and no run dropped frames.

diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index a1a3c29..d94950d 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -1877,10 +1877,13 @@ Video
             Enable vdpau decoding for h264 and mpeg2 only.
 
 ``--hwdec-threads=<N>``
-    Number of threads used for hardware decoding (default: 4). This, as opposed
-    to vd-queue, enables frame and slice threading in libavcodec. It can help
-    with pipelining the decoding process and improve performance. The exact
-    behavior depends on the hardware decoder API used.
+    Number of threads used for hardware decoding (default: 4, 1 on Apple
+    platforms). This, as opposed to vd-queue, enables frame and slice threading
+    in libavcodec. It can help with pipelining the decoding process and improve
+    performance. The exact behavior depends on the hardware decoder API used.
+    VideoToolbox decodes one frame at a time whatever the thread count, so
+    there extra threads gain no throughput and each holds back one more
+    decoded surface.
 
     If this is set to 0, the number of threads will be automatically determined
     by the number of CPU cores available.
diff --git a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
index 2c681e5..4b7b76e 100644
--- a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
+++ b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
@@ -171,7 +171,15 @@ const struct m_sub_options hwdec_conf = {
         // for example, if vo_gpu increases the number of reference surfaces for
         // interpolation, this value has to be increased too.
         .hwdec_extra_frames = 6,
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        // VideoToolbox, the only hardware decoder there, decodes one frame
+        // at a time: its hwaccels are not thread-safe, so frame threads gain
+        // no decode throughput, while each holds back another decoded
+        // surface (20 MB for a 4K P010 picture).
+        .hwdec_threads = 1,
+#else
         .hwdec_threads = 4,
+#endif
     },
 };
 
